                                "sense_id": "68af582b-b2ed-33e8-8b8b-717275e773e4",
                                "text": "a yawning chasm; the shark's yawning jaws"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e251e668-b921-47d7-a64a-a371ade9f84f",
                                "sense_id": "68af582b-b2ed-33e8-8b8b-717275e773e4",
                                "text": "That experience really taught me something. That deep down inside, I am broken, and that I'm using work to plaster over some yawning gap within myself."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4e3a4c79-ee98-448a-8c55-c74c55238153",
                                "sense_id": "68af582b-b2ed-33e8-8b8b-717275e773e4",
                                "text": "The yawning gap in neuroscientists’ understanding of their topic is in the intermediate scale of the brain’s anatomy. Science has a passable knowledge of how individual nerve cells, known as neurons, work. It also knows which visible lobes and ganglia of the brain do what."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d975f578-4596-4129-8b95-fc0387f5a712",
                                "sense_id": "68af582b-b2ed-33e8-8b8b-717275e773e4",
                                "text": "But always and ever there is a yawning chasm below[.]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
